  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection of Civilians and Peacebuilding in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Civilian Protection and Supporting Peacebuilding in South Sudan

 by engaging armed actors and de-factor authorities. 
The project seeks to strengthen the protection of civilians and contribute to sustainable peace in South Sudan by engaging armed actors and de facto authorities. Its main objective is to increase knowledge, awareness, and compliance with International Humanitarian Law (IHL) among armed actors and key civilian stakeholders in Upper Nile, Warrap, and Jonglei&#x2014;three of the states most affected by violence.

By promoting greater respect for humanitarian norms, the project aims to reduce insecurity and enhance the safety, dignity, and protection of civilians in conflict-affected areas. Strengthened adherence to IHL by armed groups and de facto authorities is expected to foster more stable and peaceful communities, contributing to broader national efforts for peace and reconciliation.</narrative>
  </description>
